# Origin response headers for bigbeardapps.com.
#
# Hostinger serves this repo with LiteSpeed, and the deploy Install Path is "/",
# so the repo root IS the web root and this file ships with every push. Setting
# the header here rather than in the Cloudflare dashboard keeps it in version
# control, visible in a diff, and impossible to forget about.
#
# WHY: the origin sends no Cache-Control on HTML, so browsers fall back to
# HEURISTIC caching — roughly 10% of the document's age since Last-Modified.
# On a page that has not changed in two days that is several hours during which
# a visitor is never told to check for a newer copy, which is why the site
# appeared to "take a while to update" on an already-visited machine.
#
# "no-cache" does NOT mean "do not store". It means revalidate before use, so
# the browser still keeps the copy and still gets a cheap 304 when nothing has
# changed — it just can never show a stale page.
#
# Assets are deliberately NOT included. site.css, launch-list.js and every
# per-app icon, poster and preview video carry a ?v=<content-hash> stamp, so
# their URL changes whenever their bytes do. Long caching is correct for them,
# and shortening it here would churn caches for nothing.
#
# Guarded by IfModule so a host without mod_headers degrades to today's
# behaviour instead of returning 500.
<IfModule mod_headers.c>
    <FilesMatch "\.html$">
        Header set Cache-Control "no-cache"
    </FilesMatch>
</IfModule>

# Tooling and data are committed (the repo root is the web root, so the host
# serves everything) but are not content. robots.txt already asks bots not to
# index /data/, /tools/ and /templates/; this actually denies them — before
# 2026-08-01 data/apps.json and tools/sync.py were publicly fetchable.
# RedirectMatch needs no module guard: mod_alias is compiled into LiteSpeed
# and Apache alike, and 404 keeps the paths indistinguishable from absent.
RedirectMatch 404 ^/(data|tools|templates)(/|$)
